// Reading one plane.
//
// Both planes have the same header shape -- a magic token, width, height, maxval
// -- and differ only in how many samples make one pixel: three for P3, one for
// P2. So this is one reader with a stride, and the two calls in spr_body are what
// distinguish colour from coverage.
//
// The maxval is read and honoured rather than assumed to be 255. ImageMagick
// writes 255 for an 8-bit image and 65535 for a 16-bit one, and a 16-bit source
// that silently imported at 1/257 brightness would be a mystery worth avoiding
// for the one multiply it costs.
//
// The sample count comes from the *header's* grid, not the plane's own width and
// height, so a plane that disagrees with the header runs out of input and reads
// zeros rather than walking off the end of the picture into the next section.

spr_plane(string src, string kd, int n) {
  string name = imp_tok(src);
  spr_magic(src, kd, name);
  spr_plane_b(src, n);
} return void;
given spr_px_ready given imp_init ("P3 1 1 255 10 20 30", "P3", 3):() then calls spr_magic:("P3 1 1 255 10 20 30", "P3", "P3")
given spr_px_ready given imp_init ("P3 1 1 255 10 20 30", "P3", 3):() then calls spr_plane_b:("P3 1 1 255 10 20 30", 3)

spr_magic(string src, string kd, string name) {
  if (name != kd) {
    err_report("stdin", 1, "expected a " + kd + " plane, got '" + name + "'");
  }
} return void;
given err_init ("x", "P3", "P3"):() then calls err_report:[0]
given err_init ("x", "P3", "Q3"):() then calls err_report:("stdin", 1, "expected a P3 plane, got 'Q3'")

// Height then maxval: the width was consumed by the caller, which is what keeps
// both of them inside three actions.
spr_max(string src) {
  imp_int(src);
  int ret_i = imp_int(src);
} return int ret_i;
given imp_init ("0 255"):(255)
given imp_init ("0 100"):(100)
